# ── Sahayak mobile runtime configuration ────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env`. Expo inlines anything prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ at build time, so
# restart the dev server (`npx expo start -c`) after changing a value — a running
# bundler will not pick it up.

# ── Supabase Auth — REQUIRED for sign-in to work at all ─────────────────────
#
# The backend verifies Supabase access tokens against this project's JWKS and
# never issues tokens of its own, so a phone OTP against Supabase is the only way
# this app can obtain a bearer. Without these the login screen says so rather
# than pretending to sign anyone in.
#
# Both come from backend/.env (SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY) and are
# the same two values web/.env uses.
#
# The PUBLISHABLE key is the right one: it identifies the project to the public
# auth endpoints, is designed to ship inside a client bundle, and grants nothing
# on its own. Never put SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY or a service-role key here — an
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ var is readable by anyone who downloads the app.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Backend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Optional. Defaults to http://10.0.2.2:8000/api/v1 in dev, which is the Android
# *emulator's* alias for the host machine — it resolves to nothing on a physical
# phone or an iOS simulator. Since receiving an OTP SMS needs a real device, set
# this to the host's LAN address when testing the sign-in flow:
#
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.20:8000/api/v1
#
# Start the backend with --host 0.0.0.0 so the phone can reach it.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=

# ── Maps (build-time, not EXPO_PUBLIC) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Read by app.config.js and baked into the native binary. Restrict the key in the
# Google Cloud console to this app's package name / bundle id and the Maps SDK.
# GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# ── Routing (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base URL of an OSRM-compatible routing service you operate. When unset, the
# partner map draws a straight connector instead of a driving route. Do not point
# this at the public OSRM demo server; it is not licensed for production traffic.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ROUTING_URL=https://routing.example.com

# ── Website ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Origin of the Sahayak website, e.g. https://sahayak.example.com. Used to open the
# Terms (/terms) and Privacy (/privacy) pages from the login and Account screens.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_WEB_URL=
